# Enterprise Architecture Baseline Lock (ENT-1)

Canonical doc: `docs/architecture/enterprise-architecture-baseline-lock.md` (ENT1-R001..ENT1-R014).
Parent freeze doc: `docs/architecture/enterprise-foundation-freeze-rules.md` (Section 2).

## Locked rules

1. Mandatory flow: `HTTP → Controller → FormRequest → Service → RepositoryInterface → Repository → Model` (authorize via Policy).
2. Controllers stay thin: request handling, authorization, delegation only.
3. Business logic lives in Services; multi-table writes use `DB::transaction`.
4. Data access goes through RepositoryInterface bindings — never bypass.
5. Branch isolation via `BranchContext`; never trust `branch_id` from request.
6. Authorization is 3-layer: route middleware/permission + Policy/Gate + `@can` UI. Hiding buttons is not authorization.
7. Migrations are additive only; never `migrate:fresh` / `db:wipe` on VPS.
8. No mutable inventory stock columns — stock derives from the ledger.
9. No full KTP/NIK or sensitive PII rendered, exported, logged, or summarized.
10. No React/Vue; stack is Blade + Alpine + Tailwind (TailAdmin).
11. No business logic in Blade.
12. No deploy shortcuts: DB backup first, `migrate --force` only, explicit cache rebuild, post-deploy smoke.
13. No feature work outside freeze scope until Enterprise Foundation Closure GO.
